for the first time a military judge has  allowed a terror detainee to speak on  the record about the cia's secret  prisons and post-9 11 interrogation  program 41 year old majeed khan a  pakistani citizen who graduated from a  maryland high school told a military  court at guantanamo bay yesterday about  brutal tactics that critics call torture  we should warn you the evidence is  graphic and may be disturbing for some  of you senior investigative  correspondent catherine herridge as at  the pentagon catherine good morning  good morning khan wore a dark suit and  sat unshackled in court yesterday's  hearing went late into the evening and  at the end khan read a 39 page statement  claiming he was sexually assaulted and  nearly drowned by his c.i.a  interrogators who he said threatened to  rape his sister  two years after 9 11 admitted al-qaeda  member majid khan was captured in  pakistan before a flight to a secret cia  prison khan said my clothes were cut off  and i was stripped nude and held down  next the americans forcibly gave me an  enema they searched my body with their  hands and took pictures of me naked i  was blindfolded and shackled someone put  a diaper on me and secured it with duct  tape  during questioning khan said he was hung  from his wrist with shackled feet barely  touching the floor the interrogators  left the room as i screamed in pain and  tried to support my weight  calling the cia facility the american  torture place khan said interrogators  went further submerging his body in an  ice bath as i struggled against drowning  then khan claimed he was sexually  assaulted while i was hanging naked  today was historic katya justin has been  representing khan as his attorney for at  least 11 years she says it took courage  for her client to give his account of  what he endured it was  very detailed and emotional and  really laid bare  the sadistic treatment that he  experienced at the hands of the cia  over a three-year period khan was  interrogated at multiple cia sites in  protest khan began hunger strikes and  claimed he was later force-fed as part  of a plea deal which included a decade  of cooperation with the government khan  admitted he joined al qaeda after his  mother's death and his father went into  debt  khan volunteered his services to khali  sheikh mohammed after 9 11 knowing he  was behind those attacks and discussed  potential plots poisoning water  reservoirs and targeting american gas  stations ton told the court i did what i  did i don't deny it i accept  responsibility and have tried to atone  for my actions under the bush  administration coley stimpson ran  detainee affairs when the men were  transferred in 2006 from the c.i.a to  the military prison at guantanamo bay as  an al qaeda terrorist  intent on seeking the death  of americans and our allies and so he's  a high value detainee he was a serious  deadly operative that's why he's  pleading guilty voluntarily at his  military commission  the continued secrecy about the  detainees treatment has been a major  impediment to resolving the remaining  guantanamo cases in his statement khan  also cast doubt on the effectiveness of  the cia program i had given up the  majority of my information from the  first day that i was captured nothing  the interrogators were doing was  effective whenever i was being tortured  i told them what i thought they wanted  to hear  under the plea agreement khan could be  transferred out of guantanamo bay to a  third country by february next year  and just to emphasize the implications  of the cia program and torture have held  up the military cases at guantanamo for  years the cia had no comment on khan's  statement but emphasized the agency shut  down its detention and interrogation  program in 2009  those details are disturbing indeed  catherine thank you
 

